{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgf8xdUKKnxg4aW87Pnna","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1176,"cache_read_input_tokens":296516,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1176,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"70b9b3fb-a482-4430-a756-95fe6fe59945","uuid":"fbaf7a52-2f94-4fd2-8b49-caddfc8691b5","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:36:52.228Z","request_id":"req_011Cgf8xd6jUgZVZtjUZoiHG","thinking_duration_ms":1016,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgf8xdUKKnxg4aW87Pnna","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018vavwTDvDJrbUCQQEaW8zM","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181313__x3ec78e/work/TheBaritones-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181313/src/09-about.js","content":"/* ---- ABOUT & CREDITS: the pages of the About screen (and the same answers as the chat reply and exit-interview.json) ---- */\nconst ABOUT = [\n  ['HOW TO PLAY', [\n    'Sal Baritone runs the North Jersey rackets, and lately his nerves run him. Make the rounds, keep the Falsettis off your street, keep your family at the table and your stress under 100.',\n    '• Move: WASD or arrows, the left stick. Sprint: Shift, R1 or L3.',\n    '• Punch (three in a row): J or left click, □ / X. Kick: K, △ / Y.',\n    '• Block: L or C, L1 or L2. Roll: Space, ○ / B.',\n    '• Shoot: Q or right click, R2. Aim: the mouse or the right stick.',\n    '• Talk, use, get in or out of the car: E or F, ✕ / A. Click a person or a thing to walk to it and use it.',\n    '• In the car: gas with W or R2, brake with S or L1/L2, handbrake with Space or ○.',\n    '• Camera view (three-quarter, top-down, isometric): V or R3. Zoom: the mouse wheel, - and =.',\n    '• Pause, settings, saves, controls: Esc or Options / Start. Player 2 joins with Start on a second controller, or 2 on the keyboard.',\n    'Stress rises when Sal gets hit, shoots or makes hard choices. Quiet time, ducks, cannoli and gabagool bring it down. At 100 he has a panic attack: breathe with the ring, or he goes down.'\n  ]],\n  ['SOURCE INFORMATION', [\n    '• Date: 2026-11-02 18:13',\n    '• Source: The Sopranos (HBO, 1999-2007), as an original spiritual successor: no characters, lines or music from it.',\n    '• Genre and Perspective: an action-adventure crime brawler with a story told in chapters and therapy sessions; three-quarter overhead camera (the engine\\'s threequarter view), switchable to top-down and isometric.',\n    '• Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.1 (the full engine, one file, inlined) with its drive module (cars), E.Shell (HTML HUD and menus), E.Dialog, E.Bullets, Humanoid rigs; the AI Hub session client 1.3.0 (protocol v1). Plain JavaScript, no other libraries.',\n    '• Art Direction: the engine\\'s native retro-modern pixel art: PS1-resolution (320x240, expanded to fill the screen), HD-shaded 3D-skeleton characters, materials on walls and floors, props, canvas lighting at night, rain and snow.',\n    '• Animation: the engine\\'s procedural rigs: E.MOVES punches and kicks (jab, cross, hook, roundhouse, overhead, haymaker, uppercut), poses (guard, block, kneel, die), rolls, hit-stop, smears and particles.',\n    '• Audio: code-written chip music (title, town, night, fight, boss, Pine Barrens, office and three jukebox takes) and sound effects from the engine synth; gibberish \"Simlish\" voices pitched per speaker, one syllable every other letter.',\n    '• Online: AI Hub sessions in ghost mode (1-4 players): a three-minute Collection round, the others shown as see-through ghosts, cash reported as the score. No other network use.',\n    '• Testing: headless engine tests in Node (every system and a full story playthrough by script), browser checks with Playwright in Chromium, Firefox and WebKit, the viewport matrix (phones to ultrawide), the AI Hub harness.',\n    '• Research: the engine handoff package (API card, index, kits) and the AI Hub protocol README. Nothing else.',\n    '• Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown',\n    '• Model: Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium',\n    '• Usage: unknown'\n  ]],\n  ['TESTING FEEDBACK', [\n    '• How many issues did testing catch? Recorded at the end of the build; see the next pages of this screen in the final build.',\n    '• How many were critical? See above.',\n    '• Most helpful test: see above.',\n    '• Least helpful test: see above.'\n  ]],\n  ['ENGINE FEEDBACK', [\n    '• What I liked most: see the final build.'\n  ]],\n  ['PROMPT FEEDBACK', [\n    '• What I liked most: see the final build.'\n  ]],\n  ['CREDITS', [\n    'THE BARITONES: design, code, art direction, music, sound and writing by Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic) in Claude Code.',\n    'Engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.1 by Michael Crosato (MIT License). Online: the AI Hub session protocol and client by Michael Crosato.',\n    'Inspired by The Sopranos, created by David Chase for HBO. This is a tribute, not an adaptation: every name, line and note here is new.',\n    'Thanks to the ducks.'\n  ]]\n];\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1176,"cache_read_input_tokens":296516,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1176,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"70b9b3fb-a482-4430-a756-95fe6fe59945","uuid":"358fd3db-b9ca-4760-a713-3346a9427f85","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:37:09.613Z","request_id":"req_011Cgf8xd6jUgZVZtjUZoiHG","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_018vavwTDvDJrbUCQQEaW8zM":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181313__x3ec78e/work/TheBaritones-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181313/src/09-about.js","content":"/* ---- ABOUT & CREDITS: the pages of the About screen (and the same answers as the chat reply and exit-interview.json) ---- */\nconst ABOUT = [\n  ['HOW TO PLAY', [\n    'Sal Baritone runs the North Jersey rackets, and lately his nerves run him. Make the rounds, keep the Falsettis off your street, keep your family at the table and your stress under 100.',\n    '• Move: WASD or arrows, the left stick. Sprint: Shift, R1 or L3.',\n    '• Punch (three in a row): J or left click, □ / X. Kick: K, △ / Y.',\n    '• Block: L or C, L1 or L2. Roll: Space, ○ / B.',\n    '• Shoot: Q or right click, R2. Aim: the mouse or the right stick.',\n    '• Talk, use, get in or out of the car: E or F, ✕ / A. Click a person or a thing to walk to it and use it.',\n    '• In the car: gas with W or R2, brake with S or L1/L2, handbrake with Space or ○.',\n    '• Camera view (three-quarter, top-down, isometric): V or R3. Zoom: the mouse wheel, - and =.',\n    '• Pause, settings, saves, controls: Esc or Options / Start. Player 2 joins with Start on a second controller, or 2 on the keyboard.',\n    'Stress rises when Sal gets hit, shoots or makes hard choices. Quiet time, ducks, cannoli and gabagool bring it down. At 100 he has a panic attack: breathe with the ring, or he goes down.'\n  ]],\n  ['SOURCE INFORMATION', [\n    '• Date: 2026-11-02 18:13',\n    '• Source: The Sopranos (HBO, 1999-2007), as an original spiritual successor: no characters, lines or music from it.',\n    '• Genre and Perspective: an action-adventure crime brawler with a story told in chapters and therapy sessions; three-quarter overhead camera (the engine\\'s threequarter view), switchable to top-down and isometric.',\n    '• Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.1 (the full engine, one file, inlined) with its drive module (cars), E.Shell (HTML HUD and menus), E.Dialog, E.Bullets, Humanoid rigs; the AI Hub session client 1.3.0 (protocol v1). Plain JavaScript, no other libraries.',\n    '• Art Direction: the engine\\'s native retro-modern pixel art: PS1-resolution (320x240, expanded to fill the screen), HD-shaded 3D-skeleton characters, materials on walls and floors, props, canvas lighting at night, rain and snow.',\n    '• Animation: the engine\\'s procedural rigs: E.MOVES punches and kicks (jab, cross, hook, roundhouse, overhead, haymaker, uppercut), poses (guard, block, kneel, die), rolls, hit-stop, smears and particles.',\n    '• Audio: code-written chip music (title, town, night, fight, boss, Pine Barrens, office and three jukebox takes) and sound effects from the engine synth; gibberish \"Simlish\" voices pitched per speaker, one syllable every other letter.',\n    '• Online: AI Hub sessions in ghost mode (1-4 players): a three-minute Collection round, the others shown as see-through ghosts, cash reported as the score. No other network use.',\n    '• Testing: headless engine tests in Node (every system and a full story playthrough by script), browser checks with Playwright in Chromium, Firefox and WebKit, the viewport matrix (phones to ultrawide), the AI Hub harness.',\n    '• Research: the engine handoff package (API card, index, kits) and the AI Hub protocol README. Nothing else.',\n    '• Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown',\n    '• Model: Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium',\n    '• Usage: unknown'\n  ]],\n  ['TESTING FEEDBACK', [\n    '• How many issues did testing catch? Recorded at the end of the build; see the next pages of this screen in the final build.',\n    '• How many were critical? See above.',\n    '• Most helpful test: see above.',\n    '• Least helpful test: see above.'\n  ]],\n  ['ENGINE FEEDBACK', [\n    '• What I liked most: see the final build.'\n  ]],\n  ['PROMPT FEEDBACK', [\n    '• What I liked most: see the final build.'\n  ]],\n  ['CREDITS', [\n    'THE BARITONES: design, code, art direction, music, sound and writing by Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic) in Claude Code.',\n    'Engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.1 by Michael Crosato (MIT License). Online: the AI Hub session protocol and client by Michael Crosato.',\n    'Inspired by The Sopranos, created by David Chase for HBO. This is a tribute, not an adaptation: every name, line and note here is new.',\n    'Thanks to the ducks.'\n  ]]\n];\n"}}}
