{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfA4TiUQ6mPAS2C1GBRN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014ZW5PBHxEQnkGjqGe31KQz","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /tmp/x3ec78e/fb.json <<'EOF'\n{\n \"testing\": [\n  \"Twelve game issues, plus five mistakes in my own tests. The game issues: the scripted panic attack never fired (stress drained to 99.9 before the check), Carmine's surrender never set the flag that ends the boss fight, the AI Hub ready() call sat on a game timer that the scene change cleared, you couldn't get out of a reversing car, moving the mouse didn't switch the prompts to the mouse, touch-only phones weren't detected in WebKit and Firefox, the pixel font had no middle dot, the therapy clock sat under the corner buttons, the moon sat under the phone menu button, banners covered fights, the SUV looked like a fridge, and Donna couldn't be clicked.\",\n  \"Three would have broken the game: the panic attack that never fired (it soft-locks chapter one), Carmine's surrender (it soft-locks the finale), and the missing ready() (AI Hub rounds never start).\",\n  \"The headless full-story playthrough: a bot plays New Story through the credits with real input taps, on two different choice paths, and it found both soft-locks.\",\n  \"The viewport matrix: 24 clean screenshots of the title with no overflow and no errors. It's reassuring, but the game draws on one canvas, so it couldn't find much.\"\n ],\n \"engine\": [\n  \"Characters with no art files: HD Humanoid rigs, E.MOVES punches and kicks with real wind-ups, and hitFx gave the brawling a good feel almost for free. The standard pause, settings, rebinding and save screens meant I spent no time on menus.\",\n  \"Yes, a few times. game.after timers are cleared on a scene change, and that ate the AI Hub ready() call. A mouse move doesn't set input.lastDevice to 'mouse' (only a button does). The pixel font has no middle dot. And I guessed facing and pose values for seated characters ('crouch' stands in for sitting).\",\n  \"The story layer: chapters as steps with check functions, a conversation queue with choices that branch, gibberish voices per speaker, and the two minigames. Also cars drawn from their heading and the gamepad axis inversion.\",\n  \"Its size: the API card, the index and the kits are a lot to take in, and the answer is often one line in a 190 KB index. Some behaviour, like timers dying with the scene and the device switching, only shows when you test.\",\n  \"I'd overhaul input.lastDevice: it should count mouse movement and stick movement, so prompts follow the device without a game wrapping input.tick.\",\n  \"Built-in axis inversion for both sticks (not just invert aim Y), plus a sit pose and a car or vehicle draw helper for ground views.\"\n ],\n \"prompt\": [\n  \"Clear, testable requirements (attract after 10 s, glyph families, the invert toggles, touch-only behaviour) and the freedom to pick a genre and a voice for the source.\",\n  \"How Multiplayer should work 'for the game on its own': I read it as local drop-in co-op plus the same Collection round the hub runs. 'Every feature in TASK.md' overlaps with the source's 'all mechanics', which leaves the scope open.\",\n  \"Fitting a whole vertical slice into one session: the story with branching choices, a boss, a car, two minigames, local and online multiplayer, and the attract mode, all tested.\",\n  \"A long real-hardware session with a DualSense on a TV, to judge the 10-foot readability and how the controller feels. Automation can only fake the pad.\"\n ]\n}\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nfb=json.load(open('/tmp/x3ec78e/fb.json'))\np='src/09-about.js'; s=open(p).read()\nqs={'testing':['How many issues did testing catch?','How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?','What was the most helpful test you ran?','What was the least helpful test you ran?'],\n'engine':['What did you like most about the engine?','Did you get stuck or guess wrong?','What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?','What was the hardest part about using the engine?','If you had to remove or overhaul one thing from the engine, what would that be?','If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?'],\n'prompt':['What did you like most about this prompt?','What was confusing?','What was the hardest thing to do?','If there was one test you could have run, what would that test be?']}\ndef page(k): return ',\\n    '.join(json.dumps('• '+q+' '+a, ensure_ascii=False) for q,a in zip(qs[k],fb[k]))\na=s.index(\"  ['TESTING FEEDBACK'\"); b=s.index(\"  ['CREDITS'\")\ns=s[:a]+\"  ['TESTING FEEDBACK', [\\n    \"+page('testing')+\"\\n  ]],\\n  ['ENGINE FEEDBACK', [\\n    \"+page('engine')+\"\\n  ]],\\n  ['PROMPT FEEDBACK', [\\n    \"+page('prompt')+\"\\n  ]],\\n\"+s[b:]\ns=s.replace(\"'• Usage: unknown'\",\"'• Usage: unknown (no token or cost meter in this session; about 40 minutes, 18:13 to 18:55)'\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"see the final\\|see above\" src/*.js; node build.mjs && node --check dist/game.js && echo OK","description":"Write final feedback into About screen; rebuild"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":588,"cache_read_input_tokens":388777,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":588,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"70b9b3fb-a482-4430-a756-95fe6fe59945","uuid":"564aabd8-1df9-47f8-a3d7-b93d319d1554","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:51:36.727Z","request_id":"req_011CgfA4TFw3PDs8KD2n7EmW","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_014ZW5PBHxEQnkGjqGe31KQz":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181313__x3ec78e/work/TheBaritones-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181313 && cat > /tmp/x3ec78e/fb.json <<'EOF'\n{\n \"testing\": [\n  \"Twelve game issues, plus five mistakes in my own tests. The game issues: the scripted panic attack never fired (stress drained to 99.9 before the check), Carmine's surrender never set the flag that ends the boss fight, the AI Hub ready() call sat on a game timer that the scene change cleared, you couldn't get out of a reversing car, moving the mouse didn't switch the prompts to the mouse, touch-only phones weren't detected in WebKit and Firefox, the pixel font had no middle dot, the therapy clock sat under the corner buttons, the moon sat under the phone menu button, banners covered fights, the SUV looked like a fridge, and Donna couldn't be clicked.\",\n  \"Three would have broken the game: the panic attack that never fired (it soft-locks chapter one), Carmine's surrender (it soft-locks the finale), and the missing ready() (AI Hub rounds never start).\",\n  \"The headless full-story playthrough: a bot plays New Story through the credits with real input taps, on two different choice paths, and it found both soft-locks.\",\n  \"The viewport matrix: 24 clean screenshots of the title with no overflow and no errors. It's reassuring, but the game draws on one canvas, so it couldn't find much.\"\n ],\n \"engine\": [\n  \"Characters with no art files: HD Humanoid rigs, E.MOVES punches and kicks with real wind-ups, and hitFx gave the brawling a good feel almost for free. The standard pause, settings, rebinding and save screens meant I spent no time on menus.\",\n  \"Yes, a few times. game.after timers are cleared on a scene change, and that ate the AI Hub ready() call. A mouse move doesn't set input.lastDevice to 'mouse' (only a button does). The pixel font has no middle dot. And I guessed facing and pose values for seated characters ('crouch' stands in for sitting).\",\n  \"The story layer: chapters as steps with check functions, a conversation queue with choices that branch, gibberish voices per speaker, and the two minigames. Also cars drawn from their heading and the gamepad axis inversion.\",\n  \"Its size: the API card, the index and the kits are a lot to take in, and the answer is often one line in a 190 KB index. Some behaviour, like timers dying with the scene and the device switching, only shows when you test.\",\n  \"I'd overhaul input.lastDevice: it should count mouse movement and stick movement, so prompts follow the device without a game wrapping input.tick.\",\n  \"Built-in axis inversion for both sticks (not just invert aim Y), plus a sit pose and a car or vehicle draw helper for ground views.\"\n ],\n \"prompt\": [\n  \"Clear, testable requirements (attract after 10 s, glyph families, the invert toggles, touch-only behaviour) and the freedom to pick a genre and a voice for the source.\",\n  \"How Multiplayer should work 'for the game on its own': I read it as local drop-in co-op plus the same Collection round the hub runs. 'Every feature in TASK.md' overlaps with the source's 'all mechanics', which leaves the scope open.\",\n  \"Fitting a whole vertical slice into one session: the story with branching choices, a boss, a car, two minigames, local and online multiplayer, and the attract mode, all tested.\",\n  \"A long real-hardware session with a DualSense on a TV, to judge the 10-foot readability and how the controller feels. Automation can only fake the pad.\"\n ]\n}\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nfb=json.load(open('/tmp/x3ec78e/fb.json'))\np='src/09-about.js'; s=open(p).read()\nqs={'testing':['How many issues did testing catch?','How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?','What was the most helpful test you ran?','What was the least helpful test you ran?'],\n'engine':['What did you like most about the engine?','Did you get stuck or guess wrong?','What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?','What was the hardest part about using the engine?','If you had to remove or overhaul one thing from the engine, what would that be?','If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?'],\n'prompt':['What did you like most about this prompt?','What was confusing?','What was the hardest thing to do?','If there was one test you could have run, what would that test be?']}\ndef page(k): return ',\\n    '.join(json.dumps('• '+q+' '+a, ensure_ascii=False) for q,a in zip(qs[k],fb[k]))\na=s.index(\"  ['TESTING FEEDBACK'\"); b=s.index(\"  ['CREDITS'\")\ns=s[:a]+\"  ['TESTING FEEDBACK', [\\n    \"+page('testing')+\"\\n  ]],\\n  ['ENGINE FEEDBACK', [\\n    \"+page('engine')+\"\\n  ]],\\n  ['PROMPT FEEDBACK', [\\n    \"+page('prompt')+\"\\n  ]],\\n\"+s[b:]\ns=s.replace(\"'• Usage: unknown'\",\"'• Usage: unknown (no token or cost meter in this session; about 40 minutes, 18:13 to 18:55)'\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"see the final\\|see above\" src/*.js; node build.mjs && node --check dist/game.js && echo OK","description":"Write final feedback into About screen; rebuild"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_014ZW5PBHxEQnkGjqGe31KQz":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181313__x3ec78e/work/TheBaritones-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181313"}}}
