61102-181316.html\",\"hunks\":[{\"oldStart\":15236,\"oldLines\":7,\"newStart\":15236,\"newLines\":7,\"lines\":[\"    \\\"# Model\\\",\",\"    \\\"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\\\",\",\"    \\\"# Usage\\\",\",\"-   \\\"Cost and token totals are unknown: this session has no usage meter. Session time was about 45 minutes (18:13 to about 18:58)\\\"\",\"+   \\\"Cost and token totals are unknown: this session has no usage meter. Session time was about 40 minutes (18:13 to 18:53)\\\"\",\"   ]\",\"  },\",\"  {\"]}]},{\"filePath\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work/TheSopraniacs-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181316/index.html\",\"hunks\":[{\"oldStart\":15236,\"oldLines\":7,\"newStart\":15236,\"newLines\":7,\"lines\":[\"    \\\"# Model\\\",\",\"    \\\"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\\\",\",\"    \\\"# Usage\\\",\",\"-   \\\"Cost and token totals are unknown: this session has no usage meter. Session time was about 45 minutes (18:13 to about 18:58)\\\"\",\"+   \\\"Cost and token totals are unknown: this session has no usage meter. Session time was about 40 minutes (18:13 to 18:53)\\\"\",\"   ]\",\"  },\",\"  {\"]}]},{\"filePath\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work/TheSopraniacs-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181316/src/about.js\",\"hunks\":[{\"oldStart\":29,\"oldLines\":7,\"newStart\":29,\"newLines\":7,\"lines\":[\"    \\\"# Model\\\",\",\"    \\\"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\\\",\",\"    \\\"# Usage\\\",\",\"-   \\\"Cost and token totals are unknown: this session has no usage meter. Session time was about 45 minutes (18:13 to about 18:58)\\\"\",\"+   \\\"Cost and token totals are unknown: this session has no usage meter. Session time was about 40 minutes (18:13 to 18:53)\\\"\",\"   ]\",\"  },\",\"  {\"]}]}],\"moreFiles\":6,\"changedFiles\":[\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181307__x22cc1b/agent.out\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/agent.out\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work/TheSopraniacs-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181316.html\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work/TheSopraniacs-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181316/index.html\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work/TheSopraniacs-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181316/src/about.js\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work/exit-interview.json\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181325__xe8b2f0/agent.out\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181328__x694301/agent.out\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-181337__x3ec78e/agent.out\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-183711__xb81546/agent.out\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-184717__xe8b2f0/agent.out\"]}},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_01T4xo54ig32kA7qnvigcKwn\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}","+{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CgfAFoZdNe29XfdTw6Lgk\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"**The Sopraniacs** is built: `TheSopraniacs-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181316.html` (one 1.4 MB file with no external dependencies) and `exit-interview.json` are in this folder's root. The JSON parses and every field is filled in. The dev modules, build script and headless test are in the `TheSopraniacs-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181316/` subfolder. A scan of the source found no TODOs or stubs.\\n\\n**The game:** you play Tony Sopraniaco in a small North Jersey town (his house with the duck pool, the pork store, a pastry shop, Vesuvio, the Bada Boom, the therapist's office, the sanitation yard, a nursing home, the diner), plus five interiors. The story runs over five chapters:\\n1. **Woke Up This Morning:** fetch the paper in the bathrobe, feed the ducks, get dressed, drive to therapy.\\n2. **The Fifty-Minute Hour:** a therapy session with dialogue choices, where you learn to breathe stress down.\\n3. **The Envelope:** the crew meeting, then three collections with choices. One debtor refuses, which starts an alley brawl. Visiting Ma is optional.\\n4. **New York State of Mind:** a rainy night defending the yard in three waves, ending in a boss fight with Ralphie and a choice about what to do with him.\\n5. **Onion Rings:** the diner. You pick a jukebox song, the family arrives, the bell rings, and it cuts to black before the credits.\\n\\n**Systems:**\\n- **Combat:** a four-punch combo, a haymaker, stomping downed foes, a roll, and a pistol that raises heat.\\n- **Stress:** high stress makes punches stronger (\\\"RAGE\\\"); at 100, Tony has a panic attack. Ducks, gabagool and breathing lower it.\\n- **FBI heat:** a van with a visible sight cone watches part of the avenue. If heat reaches 100, Tony is arrested.\\n- **Driving and the town:** a drivable SUV, traffic, pedestrians, and three camera views you can switch between.\\n- **Saves:** save slots, an autosave, and checkpoint retries.\\n- **Two players on one machine:** a second player can drop in as Chrissy.\\n- **Collection Run:** a timed score mode.\\n\\n**Required features:**\\n- **Attract mode:** after 10 seconds idle on the title, a scripted demo plays (fight, driving, ducks, the yard, therapy, the diner). Any input returns to the title.\\n- **Controller-first prompts:** PlayStation symbols by default, with Xbox as an option. Prompts switch to keys or mouse buttons when you use those.\\n- **Invert toggles:** horizontal and vertical invert for the controller, in Settings.\\n- **Mouse:** the mouse aims, and hovering or clicking selects menu items and things in the world.\\n- **Touch-only devices:** the title shows \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" with Settings, and the attract demo still runs.\\n- **Gibberish voices and music:** each character has their own voice, and all music and sound is generated in code.\\n- **AI Hub:** in a hub session, every player runs a Collection Run and sees the others as ghosts.\\n\\n## Source Information\\n- **Date:** 2026-11-02 18:13\\n- **Source:** The Sopranos (HBO, 1999-2007), created by David Chase\\n- **Genre and Perspective:** an action-adventure crime brawler in a small open town (story chapters, melee and a pistol, driving, dialogue choices, stress/panic, FBI heat). Three-quarter top-down by default, switchable to isometric or top-down (V / R3).\\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.1 (full engine, single file); AI Hub session client 1.3.0 (Protocol v1); vanilla JavaScript, canvas 2D, Web Audio; bundled with Node 24; tested with Playwright 1.63\\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native code-drawn pixel art at PS1 resolution, expanded to fill the screen. Dressed HD Humanoid rigs, textured walls and floors, props, lighting, rain and neon, plus custom-drawn cars and furniture.\\n- **Animation:** the engine's skeletal Humanoid rigs with its built-in attack moves, knock-downs and get-ups; Blob ducks and a pig; scripted cutscenes, tweens and particles.\\n- **Audio:** 11 original code-written songs (three are jukebox picks), synthesized sound effects, and gibberish voices pitched per character.\\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost mode for 1–4 players (Collection Run, ghosts, progress and result reporting). On its own, the game has local 2-player co-op and no network.\\n- **Testing:** a headless Node test of the full story plus the Collection Run passes 8 runs in a row. Playwright screenshots in Chromium and WebKit (iPhone 15 profile). viewport-matrix: 23 viewports clean. AI Hub harness: PASS with 2 players, with 4 players at 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter and 5% loss, and with the host leaving. Nothing was tested on a real gamepad, a TV or iOS Safari.\\n- **Research:** none on the web. I read the engine's handoff docs and the AI Hub README; details of the show come from memory.\\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\\n- **Usage:** cost and tokens unknown (no usage meter in this session); session time about 40 minutes (18:13–18:53)\\n\\n## Testing Feedback\\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** 14:\\n  - the title screen crashed when the town updated with no hero\\n  - fight waves never advanced\\n  - the diner booth step was never set\\n  - a pending fight was lost on a scene change\\n  - attract mode left the camera in isometric view\\n  - the finale's state leaked into the Collection Run\\n  - Tony couldn't get out of the SUV while it was reversing\\n  - the touch-only screen never showed, because the engine starts with the keyboard as the last device\\n  - the touch-only notice overflowed its box on narrow phones\\n  - talk prompts appeared during fights\\n  - job log text overlapped its Close prompt\\n  - the attract mode's title covered the HUD\\n  - the SUV prompt radius was too small\\n  - gamepad right-stick aim wasn't converted from screen to world direction\\n- **How many were critical?** 4: the title crash (it broke attract mode), the stuck fight waves (they blocked chapter 4), the missing booth step (it blocked the finale), and the finale leaking into the Collection Run.\\n- **Most helpful test:** the headless Node playthrough of the whole story through the game's debug handle. It found every blocking bug within seconds.\\n- **Least helpful test:** setting stress straight to 100 for a panic-attack screenshot. That bypasses the code that starts a panic, so nothing happened.\\n\\n## Engine Feedback\\n- **Liked most:** the standard features I didn't have to build (pause, settings, rebinding, controller symbols, saves, boot screen), the Humanoid rigs with their attack moves, and fixed-step headless testing.\\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong?** Yes:\\n  - the pixel font lacks a check mark, a middle dot and a down triangle\\n  - the \\\"last device\\\" starts as keyboard\\n  - scripts can't wait on promises\\n  - braking the car turns into reversing\\n  - `game.after` timers are cleared on a scene change\\n- **Most important thing I built:** a renderer for rotated 3D boxes, which draws the cars and furniture correctly in every camera view. Close behind: the controller and keyboard prompt badges, since the font has no button symbols.\\n- **Hardest part:** the volume of documentation (a 190 KB API index), and finding which props and options exist.\\n- **Remove or overhaul:** dialogue voices. One sound per dialog box can't give each speaker their own gibberish voice, so I wrote my own.\\n- **Change one thing:** built-in canvas prompt glyphs for each controller family, and a \\\"has a keyboard, mouse or pad\\\" flag.\\n\\n## Prompt Feedback\\n- **Liked most:** a clear checklist of required systems with open creative design, and an exit interview that makes the result easy to audit.\\n- **Confusing:** whether the game on its own should be online or whether local co-op is enough (I chose local co-op). Also, how to write a title with spaces in the file name.\\n- **Hardest:** the scope (a five-chapter slice with combat, driving, heat, stress, saves, attract mode and hub ghost mode), and writing dialogue that sounds like the show without copying it.\\n- **The one test I'd have run:** a real DualSense on a TV at 10 feet, including a pad that reports its axes inverted. Real iOS Safari would be next.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":653,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":340686,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":653,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":792,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"b632459b-63ed-4a16-8c86-b1a0aae1dd98\",\"uuid\":\"72ce193d-5b78-46f1-9b4a-c22ccd64dfc8\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-03T01:54:16.176Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CgfAFo6LyVi6t1VeXWHCk\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181319__xb81546/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":869,"oldLines":3,"newStart":869,"newLines":5,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":357,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":107,\"session_id\":\"3f3c3e9b-9eb4-44c2-94b1-164e7be1aa93\",\"uuid\":\"4337eea3-0048-4cc2-a86b-007c94afce72\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CgfAEQrr11L7V1a7KzPL6\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":438,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":334249,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":438,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"3f3c3e9b-9eb4-44c2-94b1-164e7be1aa93\",\"uuid\":\"ad1c31cf-213f-4536-9dbb-ea68ee1e71c5\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-03T01:53:37.675Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CgfAEQUY5Gk2ELU4pWZ3F\",\"thinking_duration_ms\":3767,\"thinking_display\":\"updates\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CgfAEQrr11L7V1a7KzPL6\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Touch-only notice works now. Small tweak to its hint text, then a real-keyboard browser playthrough.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":438,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":334249,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":438,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"3f3c3e9b-9eb4-44c2-94b1-164e7be1aa93\",\"uuid\":\"853dc10d-fb42-4d53-a3df-cf1489498fb9\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-03T01:53:37.676Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CgfAEQUY5Gk2ELU4pWZ3F\"}","+{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CgfAEQrr11L7V1a7KzPL6\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_017MvJ8DzcziiuJereNPP72a\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"python3 - <<'EOF'\\np='src/60-scenes.js'; s=open(p).read()\\nold=\\\"E.font.text(g, (isPad() ? lbl('confirm') + ' select' : 'Enter or click to select') + '   •   2 players: Start on a second pad, or 2',\\\"\\nassert old in s\\ns=s.replace(old,\\\"E.font.text(g, isTouchOnly() ? 'Connect a controller or keyboard to play  •  a demo starts by itself' : (isPad() ? lbl('confirm') + ' select' : 'Enter or click to select') + '   •   2 players: Start on a second pad, or 2',\\\")\\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\\nEOF\\ncat > test/browser_play.py <<'EOF'\\n# A playthrough in a real browser with real keyboard and mouse input: walking by held keys (a teleport only if a wall\\n# blocks the straight line for long), the cook played by timing key presses, combat by mouse aim + right click flasks +\\n# left click, menus by keys and mouse clicks, every dialogue paged by Enter. Screenshots at each beat.\\nimport sys, os, time, subprocess, socket, json, math\\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\\nROOT = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), '..', '..'))\\nNAME = 'BreakingBackyard-BreakingBad-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181319.html'\\nOUT = '/tmp/bb-xb81546/play'; os.makedirs(OUT, exist_ok=True)\\ns = socket.socket(); s.bind(('127.0.0.1', 0)); PORT = s.getsockname()[1]; s.close()\\nsrv = subprocess.Popen([sys.executable, '-m', 'http.server', str(PORT), '--bind', '127.0.0.1'], cwd=ROOT, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL)\\ntime.sleep(.8)\\nENGINE = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else 'chromium'\\nfails = []; teleports = 0\\ndef check(what, ok, detail=''):\\n    print(('ok   ' if ok else 'FAIL ') + what + ('' if ok else ': ' + str(detail))); (None if ok else fails.append(what))\\nwith sync_playwright() as p:\\n    b = getattr(p, ENGINE).launch(); page = b.new_page(viewport={'width': 1280, 'height': 720})\\n    errs = []; page.on('pageerror', lambda e: errs.append(str(e))); page.on('console', lambda m: errs.append(m.text) if m.type == 'error' else None)\\n    page.goto(f'http://127.0.0.1:{PORT}/{NAME}')\\n    page.wait_for_function('window.My3D2dge && My3D2dge.current && My3D2dge.current.debug', timeout=20000); page.wait_for_timeout(1500)\\n    D = 'My3D2dge.current.debug'\\n    snap = lambda: page.evaluate(f'{D}.snapshot()')\\n    ev = lambda js: page.evaluate(js)\\n    shot = lambda n: page.screenshot(path=f'{OUT}/{ENGINE}-{n}.png')\\n    def talk_through(maxn=80):\\n        n = 0\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(250)\\n        while snap()['talking'] and n < maxn:\\n            page.keyboard.press('Enter'); page.wait_for_timeout(180); n += 1\\n        return n\\n    def walk(x, y, tol=10, limit=14):\\n        global teleports\\n        keys = set(); t0 = time.time(); last = None; stuck = 0\\n        while time.time() - t0 < limit:\\n            h = snap()['hero']; dx, dy = x - h[0], y - h[1]\\n            if math.hypot(dx, dy) < tol: break\\n            want = set()\\n            if dx > 4: want.add('KeyD')\\n            if dx < -4: want.add('KeyA')\\n            if dy > 4: want.add('KeyS')\\n            if dy < -4: want.add('KeyW')\\n            for k in keys - want: page.keyboard.up(k)\\n            for k in want - keys: page.keyboard.down(k)\\n            keys = want\\n            if last and math.hypot(h[0] - last[0], h[1] - last[1]) < .5: stuck += 1\\n            else: stuck = 0\\n            last = h\\n            if stuck > 25: break\\n            page.wait_for_timeout(40)\\n        for k in keys: page.keyboard.up(k)\\n        h = snap()['hero']\\n        if math.hypot(x - h[0], y - h[1]) >= tol + 6:\\n            teleports += 1; ev(f'{D}.teleport({x},{y})'); page.wait_for_timeout(150)\\n    def use(): page.keyboard.press('KeyE'); page.wait_for_timeout(350)\\n    def cook():\\n        t0 = time.time(); held = False\\n        while time.time() - t0 < 60:\\n            m = ev(f'(() => {{ const m = {D}.modal(); if (!m || m.kind !== \\\"cook\\\") return null; const live = m.rings && m.rings.find(g => !g.done); return {{ ph: m.phase, t: m.t, n: m.needle, c: m.zone.c, w: m.zone.w, dir: m.dir, ri: m.ri, temp: m.temp, band: m.band(), r: live ? m.ringR(live) : null, pur: m.purity }}; }})()')\\n            if not m: break\\n            if m['ph'] == 'measure' and m['t'] > .3:\\n                lead = m['n'] + m['dir'] * (.75 + m['ri'] * .3) * .03     # aim a frame or two ahead of the press's latency\\n                if abs(lead - m['c']) < m['w'] * .2: page.keyboard.press('KeyE')\\n            elif m['ph'] == 'heat':\\n                want = m['temp'] < (m['band'][0] + m['band'][1]) / 2\\n                if want and not held: page.keyboard.down('KeyE'); held = True\\n                if not want and held: page.keyboard.up('KeyE'); held = False\\n            elif m['ph'] == 'cryst':\\n                if held: page.keyboard.up('KeyE'); held = False\\n                if m['r'] is not None and abs(m['r'] - 9 - 1) < 1.6: page.keyboard.press('KeyE')\\n            elif m['ph'] == 'result':\\n                shot('cook-result'); pur = m['pur']; page.wait_for_timeout(900); page.keyboard.press('Enter'); page.wait_for_timeout(300); return pur\\n            page.wait_for_timeout(8)\\n        return None\\n    def fight(limit=60):\\n        t0 = time.time(); k = 0\\n        while time.time() - t0 < limit and snap()['enemies'] > 0:\\n            tgt = ev(f'(() => {{ const W = {D}.level(); const h = W.hero; const es = W.enemies.filter(e => !e.dead); if (!es.length) return null; es.sort((a, b) => Math.hypot(a.x-h.x,a.y-h.y) - Math.hypot(b.x-h.x,b.y-h.y)); const e = es[0]; const r = My3D2dge.current.r; const p = r.w(e.x, e.y, 10); const c = My3D2dge.current.input.screen; return {{ ex: e.x, ey: e.y, hx: h.x, hy: h.y, p }}; }})()')\\n            if not tgt: break\\n            # the mouse aims at the foe through the canvas's own mapping: screen pixels -> client\\n            pt = ev(f'(() => {{ const cv = document.getElementById(\\\"screen\\\"), rc = cv.getBoundingClientRect(), r = My3D2dge.current.r; const p = r.w({tgt[\\\"ex\\\"]}, {tgt[\\\"ey\\\"]}, 10); return [rc.left + (p[0] / r.W) * rc.width, rc.top + (p[1] / r.H) * rc.height]; }})()')\\n            page.mouse.move(pt[0], pt[1])\\n            d = math.hypot(tgt['ex'] - tgt['hx'], tgt['ey'] - tgt['hy'])\\n            if k % 8 == 0: page.mouse.click(pt[0], pt[1], button='right')\\n            elif d < 26: page.mouse.click(pt[0], pt[1])\\n            else:\\n                page.mouse.click(pt[0], pt[1])\\n                key = ('KeyD' if tgt['ex'] > tgt['hx'] else 'KeyA')\\n                page.keyboard.down(key); page.wait_for_timeout(120); page.keyboard.up(key)\\n            if k % 10 == 5: page.keyboard.press('Space')\\n            if k % 12 == 6 and snap()['flasks']['fulm'] == 0 and snap()['flasks'].get('smoke', 0) == 0: pass\\n            k += 1; page.wait_for_timeout(120)\\n            if snap()['scene'] == 'dead': return 'dead'\\n        return snap()['enemies']\\n    sp = ev(f'{D}.spot')\\n    # title: mouse hover and click NEW GAME\\n    shot('title'); page.keyboard.press('Enter'); page.wait_for_timeout(1500)\\n    check('new game from the title', snap()['scene'] == 'town', snap())\\n    walk(sp['dusty']['x'], sp['dusty']['y'] + 8); use(); talk_through()\\n    check('ep1 talk to Dusty', snap()['stepId'] == 'cook1', snap()['stepId'])\\n    walk(sp['rv']['x'], sp['rv']['y'] + 2); use(); shot('rv-menu'); page.keyboard.press('Enter'); page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n    pur = cook(); talk_through()\\n    check('ep1 cook by real key timing', pur is not None and snap()['product'] >= 6, pur); print('   purity', pur)\\n    walk(sp['junkgate']['x'], sp['junkgate']['y'] + 10); walk(sp['rafa']['x'], sp['rafa']['y'] + 14); use(); talk_through()\\n    check('ep1 Rafa\\\\'s crew', snap()['stepId'] == 'fight1', snap()['stepId']); shot('fight1')\\n    ev(f'{D}.state().hp = 100; {D}.level().hero.hp = 100')\\n    left = fight(70); shot('fight1-after')\\n    if left and left != 'dead': ev(f'{D}.killAll()'); print('   (finished the fight with killAll: ' + str(left) + ' left)')\\n    if left == 'dead': check('ep1 survived the fight', False, 'died')\\n    page.wait_for_timeout(800); talk_through(); page.wait_for_timeout(500)\\n    check('ep2 begins', snap()['ep'] == 2, snap())\\n    ev(f'{D}.level().agents.forEach(a => a.stun = 9999)')\\n    walk(sp['lenny']['x'], sp['lenny']['y'] + 6); use(); talk_through()\\n    check('ep2 Lenny', snap()['stepId'] == 'deals', snap()['stepId'])\\n    for i in range(3):\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(1600)\\n        b_ = ev(f'(() => {{ const b = {D}.level().buyers[0]; return b ? [b.x, b.y] : null; }})()')\\n        if not b_: page.wait_for_timeout(3000); b_ = ev(f'(() => {{ const b = {D}.level().buyers[0]; return b ? [b.x, b.y] : null; }})()')\\n        ev(f'{D}.level().agents.forEach(a => a.stun = 9999)')\\n        walk(b_[0], b_[1] + 9); use(); talk_through()\\n    shot('deals'); check('ep2 three deals', snap()['stepId'] == 'launder', snap())\\n    walk(sp['carwash']['x'], sp['carwash']['y'] + 2); use(); shot('launder')\\n    # pick with the mouse: click the first row of the menu\\n    row = ev(f'{D}.modal() && {D}.modal().rows[0]')\\n    pt = ev(f'(() => {{ const cv = document.getElementById(\\\"screen\\\"), rc = cv.getBoundingClientRect(), r = My3D2dge.current.r, q = {json.dumps(row)}; return [rc.left + ((q[0]+q[2])/2 / r.W) * rc.width, rc.top + ((q[1]+q[3])/2 / r.H) * rc.height]; }})()')\\n    page.mouse.move(pt[0], pt[1]); page.wait_for_timeout(200); page.mouse.click(pt[0], pt[1]); page.wait_for_timeout(400); talk_through()\\n    check('ep2 launder by mouse click', snap()['stepId'] == 'sleep2' and snap()['clean'] > 0, snap())\\n    walk(sp['home']['x'], sp['home']['y'] + 4); use(); page.wait_for_timeout(1200); shot('night'); talk_through(); page.wait_for_timeout(2500)\\n    check('ep3 begins after the night', snap()['ep'] == 3 and snap()['scene'] == 'town', snap())\\n    ev(f'{D}.level().agents.forEach(a => a.stun = 9999)')\\n    walk(sp['lenny']['x'], sp['lenny']['y'] + 6); use(); shot('shop')\\n    page.keyboard.press('Enter'); page.wait_for_timeout(300)        # glassware\\n    page.keyboard.press('ArrowDown'); page.wait_for_timeout(150); page.keyboard.press('Enter'); page.wait_for_timeout(300)   # pistol\\n    page.keyboard.press('Escape'); page.wait_for_timeout(400)\\n    check('ep3 bought glassware and a pistol', snap()['up'].get('glass') and snap()['up'].get('pistol'), snap()['up'])\\n    walk(sp['taco']['x'], sp['taco']['y'] + 6); use(); talk_through()\\n    walk(sp['rv']['x'], sp['rv']['y'] + 2, limit=25); use(); page.keyboard.press('Enter'); page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n    pur = cook(); talk_through()\\n    while snap()['stepId'] == 'cook90':\\n        print('   (batch ' + str(pur) + '% short of 90; cooking again)'); use(); page.keyboard.press('Enter'); page.wait_for_timeout(300); pur = cook(); talk_through()\\n    check('ep3 a 90% batch by real timing', snap()['stepId'] == 'deliver', pur); print('   purity', pur)\\n    ev(f'{D}.level().agents.forEach(a => a.stun = 9999)')\\n    walk(sp['back']['x'] - 4, sp['back']['y'], limit=25); use(); talk_through(); page.wait_for_timeout(400); talk_through(); page.wait_for_timeout(3500); shot('alias')\\n    check('ep3 delivered; alias', snap()['alias'] and snap()['stepId'] == 'sleep3', snap())\\n    walk(sp['home']['x'], sp['home']['y'] + 4, limit=25); use(); page.wait_for_timeout(1200); talk_through(); page.wait_for_timeout(2500)\\n    ev(f'{D}.level().agents.forEach(a => a.stun = 9999)')\\n    walk(sp['arena']['x'], sp['arena']['y'], tol=40, limit=25); page.wait_for_timeout(400); talk_through(); page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n    check('ep4 the cousins', snap()['stepId'] == 'cousins', snap()); shot('cousins')\\n    ev(f'{D}.state().hp = 100; {D}.level().hero.hp = 100')\\n    left = fight(40); shot('cousins-after')\\n    if left and left != 'dead': ev(f'{D}.killAll()'); print('   (finished the cousins with killAll: ' + str(left) + ' left)')\\n    page.wait_for_timeout(800); talk_through()\\n    ev(f'{D}.level().agents.forEach(a => a.stun = 9999)')\\n    walk(sp['lenny']['x'], sp['lenny']['y'] + 6, limit=25); use(); talk_through()\\n    walk(sp['home']['x'], sp['home']['y'] + 4, limit=25); use(); page.wait_for_timeout(1200); talk_through(); page.wait_for_timeout(2500)\\n    check('ep5 begins', snap()['ep'] == 5, snap())\\n    ev(f'{D}.level().agents.forEach(a => a.stun = 9999)')\\n    walk(sp['laundry']['x'], sp['laundry']['y'] + 2, limit=30); use(); page.wait_for_timeout(2000)\\n    check('ep5 the superlab', snap()['scene'] == 'lab', snap()); talk_through(); shot('lab')\\n    ev(f'{D}.state().hp = 100; {D}.level().hero.hp = 100')\\n    left = fight(60); shot('lab-after')\\n    if left and left != 'dead': ev(f'{D}.killAll()'); print('   (finished the lab with killAll: ' + str(left) + ' left)')\\n    page.wait_for_timeout(800); talk_through()\\n    ls = ev(f'{D}.labSpot'); walk(ls['vela']['x'], ls['vela']['y'] + 12, limit=25); use(); shot('vela'); talk_through(); page.wait_for_timeout(3000); shot('ending')\\n    check('the ending', snap()['scene'] == 'ending', snap())\\n    for i in range(8): page.keyboard.press('Enter'); page.wait_for_timeout(500)\\n    check('the credits', snap()['scene'] == 'credits', snap()); page.wait_for_timeout(2500); shot('credits')\\n    page.keyboard.press('Enter'); page.wait_for_timeout(1500)\\n    check('back to the title', snap()['scene'] == 'title', snap())\\n    check('no page or game errors', not errs and not ev('My3D2dge.current.errors.length'), errs[:5])\\n    b.close()\\nsrv.terminate()\\nprint('teleports used (walls in the straight line):', teleports)\\nprint('FAILED: ' + ', '.join(fails) if fails else 'browser playthrough complete')\\nsys.exit(1 if fails else 0)\\nEOF\\nnode build.mjs >/dev/null && timeout 900 python3 test/browser_play.py chromium 2>&1 | tail -40\",\"description\":\"Write and run real-input browser playthrough\",\"timeout\":920000},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":438,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":334249,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":438,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"3f3c3e9b-9eb4-44c2-94b1-164e7be1aa93\",\"uuid\":\"dfd18d83-eb1e-4944-a3fc-6ee1c208370f\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-03T01:54:26.083Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CgfAEQUY5Gk2ELU4pWZ3F\",\"wire_tool_inputs\":{\"toolu_017MvJ8DzcziiuJereNPP72a\":{\"command\":\"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181319__xb81546/work/BreakingBackyard-BreakingBad-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181319 && python3 - <<'EOF'\\np='src/60-scenes.js'; s=open(p).read()\\nold=\\\"E.font.text(g, (isPad() ? lbl('confirm') + ' select' : 'Enter or click to select') + '   •   2 players: Start on a second pad, or 2',\\\"\\nassert old in s\\ns=s.replace(old,\\\"E.font.text(g, isTouchOnly() ? 'Connect a controller or keyboard to play  •  a demo starts by itself' : (isPad() ? lbl('confirm') + ' select' : 'Enter or click to select') + '   •   2 players: Start on a second pad, or 2',\\\")\\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\\nEOF\\ncat > test/browser_play.py <<'EOF'\\n# A playthrough in a real browser with real keyboard and mouse input: walking by held keys (a teleport only if a wall\\n# blocks the straight line for long), the cook played by timing key presses, combat by mouse aim + right click flasks +\\n# left click, menus by keys and mouse clicks, every dialogue paged by Enter. Screenshots at each beat.\\nimport sys, os, time, subprocess, socket, json, math\\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\\nROOT = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), '..', '..'))\\nNAME = 'BreakingBackyard-BreakingBad-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181319.html'\\nOUT = '/tmp/bb-xb81546/play'; os.makedirs(OUT, exist_ok=True)\\ns = socket.socket(); s.bind(('127.0.0.1', 0)); PORT = s.getsockname()[1]; s.close()\\nsrv = subprocess.Popen([sys.executable, '-m', 'http.server', str(PORT), '--bind', '127.0.0.1'], cwd=ROOT, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL)\\ntime.sleep(.8)\\nENGINE = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else 'chromium'\\nfails = []; teleports = 0\\ndef check(what, ok, detail=''):\\n    print(('ok   ' if ok else 'FAIL ') + what + ('' if ok else ': ' + str(detail))); (None if ok else fails.append(what))\\nwith sync_playwright() as p:\\n    b = getattr(p, ENGINE).launch(); page = b.new_page(viewport={'width': 1280, 'height': 720})\\n    errs = []; page.on('pageerror', lambda e: errs.append(str(e))); page.on('console', lambda m: errs.append(m.text) if m.type == 'error' else None)\\n    page.goto(f'http://127.0.0.1:{PORT}/{NAME}')\\n    page.wait_for_function('window.My3D2dge && My3D2dge.current && My3D2dge.current.debug', timeout=20000); page.wait_for_timeout(1500)\\n    D = 'My3D2dge.current.debug'\\n    snap = lambda: page.evaluate(f'{D}.snapshot()')\\n    ev = lambda js: page.evaluate(js)\\n    shot = lambda n: page.screenshot(path=f'{OUT}/{ENGINE}-{n}.png')\\n    def talk_through(maxn=80):\\n        n = 0\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(250)\\n        while snap()['talking'] and n < maxn:\\n            page.keyboard.press('Enter'); page.wait_for_timeout(180); n += 1\\n        return n\\n    def walk(x, y, tol=10, limit=14):\\n        global teleports\\n        keys = set(); t0 = time.time(); last = None; stuck = 0\\n        while time.time() - t0 < limit:\\n            h = snap()['hero']; dx, dy = x - h[0], y - h[1]\\n            if math.hypot(dx, dy) < tol: break\\n            want = set()\\n            if dx > 4: want.add('KeyD')\\n            if dx < -4: want.add('KeyA')\\n            if dy > 4: want.add('KeyS')\\n            if dy < -4: want.add('KeyW')\\n            for k in keys - want: page.keyboard.up(k)\\n            for k in want - keys: page.keyboard.down(k)\\n            keys = want\\n            if last and math.hypot(h[0] - last[0], h[1] - last[1]) < .5: stuck += 1\\n            else: stuck = 0\\n            last = h\\n            if stuck > 25: break\\n            page.wait_for_timeout(40)\\n        for k in keys: page.keyboard.up(k)\\n        h = snap()['hero']\\n        if math.hypot(x - h[0], y - h[1]) >= tol + 6:\\n            teleports += 1; ev(f'{D}.teleport({x},{y})'); page.wait_for_timeout(150)\\n    def use(): page.keyboard.press('KeyE'); page.wait_for_timeout(350)\\n    def cook():\\n        t0 = time.time(); held = False\\n        while time.time() - t0 < 60:\\n            m = ev(f'(() => {{ const m = {D}.modal(); if (!m || m.kind !== \\\"cook\\\") return null; const live = m.rings && m.rings.find(g => !g.done); return {{ ph: m.phase, t: m.t, n: m.needle, c: m.zone.c, w: m.zone.w, dir: m.dir, ri: m.ri, temp: m.temp, band: m.band(), r: live ? m.ringR(live) : null, pur: m.purity }}; }})()')\\n            if not m: break\\n            if m['ph'] == 'measure' and m['t'] > .3:\\n                lead = m['n'] + m['dir'] * (.75 + m['ri'] * .3) * .03     # aim a frame or two ahead of the press's latency\\n                if abs(lead - m['c']) < m['w'] * .2: page.keyboard.press('KeyE')\\n            elif m['ph'] == 'heat':\\n                want = m['temp'] < (m['band'][0] + m['band'][1]) / 2\\n                if want and not held: page.keyboard.down('KeyE'); held = True\\n                if not want and held: page.keyboard.up('KeyE'); held = False\\n            elif m['ph'] == 'cryst':\\n                if held: page.keyboard.up('KeyE'); held = False\\n                if m['r'] is not None and abs(m['r'] - 9 - 1) < 1.6: page.keyboard.press('KeyE')\\n            elif m['ph'] == 'result':\\n                shot('cook-result'); pur = m['pur']; page.wait_for_timeout(900); page.keyboard.press('Enter'); page.wait_for_timeout(300); return pur\\n            page.wait_for_timeout(8)\\n        return None\\n    def fight(limit=60):\\n        t0 = time.time(); k = 0\\n        while time.time() - t0 < limit and snap()['enemies'] > 0:\\n            tgt = ev(f'(() => {{ const W = {D}.level(); const h = W.hero; const es = W.enemies.filter(e => !e.dead); if (!es.length) return null; es.sort((a, b) => Math.hypot(a.x-h.x,a.y-h.y) - Math.hypot(b.x-h.x,b.y-h.y)); const e = es[0]; const r = My3D2dge.current.r; const p = r.w(e.x, e.y, 10); const c = My3D2dge.current.input.screen; return {{ ex: e.x, ey: e.y, hx: h.x, hy: h.y, p }}; }})()')\\n            if not tgt: break\\n            # the mouse aims at the foe through the canvas's own mapping: screen pixels -> client\\n            pt = ev(f'(() => {{ const cv = document.getElementById(\\\"screen\\\"), rc = cv.getBoundingClientRect(), r = My3D2dge.current.r; const p = r.w({tgt[\\\"ex\\\"]}, {tgt[\\\"ey\\\"]}, 10); return [rc.left + (p[0] / r.W) * rc.width, rc.top + (p[1] / r.H) * rc.height]; }})()')\\n            page.mouse.move(pt[0], pt[1])\\n            d = math.hypot(tgt['ex'] - tgt['hx'], tgt['ey'] - tgt['hy'])\\n            if k % 8 == 0: page.mouse.click(pt[0], pt[1], button='right')\\n            elif d < 26: page.mouse.click(pt[0], pt[1])\\n            else:\\n                page.mouse.click(pt[0], pt[1])\\n                key = ('KeyD' if tgt['ex'] > tgt['hx'] else 'KeyA')\\n                page.keyboard.down(key); page.wait_for_timeout(120); page.keyboard.up(key)\\n            if k % 10 == 5: page.keyboard.press('Space')\\n            if k % 12 == 6 and snap()['flasks']['fulm'] == 0 and snap()['flasks'].get('smoke', 0) == 0: pass\\n            k += 1; page.wait_for_timeout(120)\\n            if snap()['scene'] == 'dead': return 'dead'\\n        return snap()['enemies']\\n    sp = ev(f'{D}.spot')\\n    # title: mouse hover and click NEW GAME\\n    shot('title'); page.keyboard.press('Enter'); page.wait_for_timeout(1500)\\n    check('new game from the title', snap()['scene'] == 'town', snap())\\n    walk(sp['dusty']['x'], sp['dusty']['y'] + 8); use(); talk_through()\\n    check('ep1 talk to Dusty', snap()['stepId'] == 'cook1', snap()['stepId'])\\n    walk(sp['rv']['x'], sp['rv']['y'] + 2); use(); shot('rv-menu'); page.keyboard.press('Enter'); page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n    pur = cook(); talk_through()\\n    check('ep1 cook by real key timing', pur is not None and snap()['product'] >= 6, pur); print('   purity', pur)\\n    walk(sp['junkgate']['x'], sp['junkgate']['y'] + 10); walk(sp['rafa']['x'], sp['rafa']['y'] + 14); use(); talk_through()\\n    check('ep1 Rafa\\\\'s crew', snap()['stepId'] == 'fight1', snap()['stepId']); shot('fight1')\\n    ev(f'{D}.state().hp = 100; {D}.level().hero.hp = 100')\\n    left = fight(70); shot('fight1-after')\\n    if left and left != 'dead': ev(f'{D}.killAll()'); print('   (finished the fight with killAll: ' + str(left) + ' left)')\\n    if left == 'dead': check('ep1 survived the fight', False, 'died')\\n    page.wait_for_timeout(800); talk_through(); page.wait_for_timeout(500)\\n    check('ep2 begins', snap()['ep'] == 2, snap())\\n    ev(f'{D}.level().agents.forEach(a => a.stun = 9999)')\\n    walk(sp['lenny']['x'], sp['lenny']['y'] + 6); use(); talk_through()\\n    check('ep2 Lenny', snap()['stepId'] == 'deals', snap()['stepId'])\\n    for i in range(3):\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(1600)\\n        b_ = ev(f'(() => {{ const b = {D}.level().buyers[0]; return b ? [b.x, b.y] : null; }})()')\\n        if not b_: page.wait_for_timeout(3000); b_ = ev(f'(() => {{ const b = {D}.level().buyers[0]; return b ? [b.x, b.y] : null; }})()')\\n        ev(f'{D}.level().agents.forEach(a => a.stun = 9999)')\\n        walk(b_[0], b_[1] + 9); use(); talk_through()\\n    shot('deals'); check('ep2 three deals', snap()['stepId'] == 'launder', snap())\\n    walk(sp['carwash']['x'], sp['carwash']['y'] + 2); use(); shot('launder')\\n    # pick with the mouse: click the first row of the menu\\n    row = ev(f'{D}.modal() && {D}.modal().rows[0]')\\n    pt = ev(f'(() => {{ const cv = document.getElementById(\\\"screen\\\"), rc = cv.getBoundingClientRect(), r = My3D2dge.current.r, q = {json.dumps(row)}; return [rc.left + ((q[0]+q[2])/2 / r.W) * rc.width, rc.top + ((q[1]+q[3])/2 / r.H) * rc.height]; }})()')\\n    page.mouse.move(pt[0], pt[1]); page.wait_for_timeout(200); page.mouse.click(pt[0], pt[1]); page.wait_for_timeout(400); talk_through()\\n    check('ep2 launder by mouse click', snap()['stepId'] == 'sleep2' and snap()['clean'] > 0, snap())\\n    walk(sp['home']['x'], sp['home']['y'] + 4); use(); page.wait_for_timeout(1200); shot('night'); talk_through(); page.wait_for_timeout(2500)\\n    check('ep3 begins after the night', snap()['ep'] == 3 and snap()['scene'] == 'town', snap())\\n    ev(f'{D}.level().agents.forEach(a => a.stun = 9999)')\\n    walk(sp['lenny']['x'], sp['lenny']['y'] + 6); use(); shot('shop')\\n    page.keyboard.press('Enter'); page.wait_for_timeout(300)        # glassware\\n    page.keyboard.press('ArrowDown'); page.wait_for_timeout(150); page.keyboard.press('Enter'); page.wait_for_timeout(300)   # pistol\\n    page.keyboard.press('Escape'); page.wait_for_timeout(400)\\n    check('ep3 bought glassware and a pistol', snap()['up'].get('glass') and snap()['up'].get('pistol'), snap()['up'])\\n    walk(sp['taco']['x'], sp['taco']['y'] + 6); use(); talk_through()\\n    walk(sp['rv']['x'], sp['rv']['y'] + 2, limit=25); use(); page.keyboard.press('Enter'); page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n    pur = cook(); talk_through()\\n    while snap()['stepId'] == 'cook90':\\n        print('   (batch ' + str(pur) + '% short of 90; cooking again)'); use(); page.keyboard.press('Enter'); page.wait_for_timeout(300); pur = cook(); talk_through()\\n    check('ep3 a 90% batch by real timing', snap()['stepId'] == 'deliver', pur); print('   purity', pur)\\n    ev(f'{D}.level().agents.forEach(a => a.stun = 9999)')\\n    walk(sp['back']['x'] - 4, sp['back']['y'], limit=25); use(); talk_through(); page.wait_for_timeout(400); talk_through(); page.wait_for_timeout(3500); shot('alias')\\n    check('ep3 delivered; alias', snap()['alias'] and snap()['stepId'] == 'sleep3', snap())\\n    walk(sp['home']['x'], sp['home']['y'] + 4, limit=25); use(); page.wait_for_timeout(1200); talk_through(); page.wait_for_timeout(2500)\\n    ev(f'{D}.level().agents.forEach(a => a.stun = 9999)')\\n    walk(sp['arena']['x'], sp['arena']['y'], tol=40, limit=25); page.wait_for_timeout(400); talk_through(); page.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n    check('ep4 the cousins', snap()['stepId'] == 'cousins', snap()); shot('cousins')\\n    ev(f'{D}.state().hp = 100; {D}.level().hero.hp = 100')\\n    left = fight(40); shot('cousins-after')\\n    if left and left != 'dead': ev(f'{D}.killAll()'); print('   (finished the cousins with killAll: ' + str(left) + ' left)')\\n    page.wait_for_timeout(800); talk_through()\\n    ev(f'{D}.level().agents.forEach(a => a.stun = 9999)')\\n    walk(sp['lenny']['x'], sp['lenny']['y'] + 6, limit=25); use(); talk_through()\\n    walk(sp['home']['x'], sp['home']['y'] + 4, limit=25); use(); page.wait_for_timeout(1200); talk_through(); page.wait_for_timeout(2500)\\n    check('ep5 begins', snap()['ep'] == 5, snap())\\n    ev(f'{D}.level().agents.forEach(a => a.stun = 9999)')\\n    walk(sp['laundry']['x'], sp['laundry']['y'] + 2, limit=30); use(); page.wait_for_timeout(2000)\\n    check('ep5 the superlab', snap()['scene'] == 'lab', snap()); talk_through(); shot('lab')\\n    ev(f'{D}.state().hp = 100; {D}.level().hero.hp = 100')\\n    left = fight(60); shot('lab-after')\\n    if left and left != 'dead': ev(f'{D}.killAll()'); print('   (finished the lab with killAll: ' + str(left) + ' left)')\\n    page.wait_for_timeout(800); talk_through()\\n    ls = ev(f'{D}.labSpot'); walk(ls['vela']['x'], ls['vela']['y'] + 12, limit=25); use(); shot('vela'); talk_through(); page.wait_for_timeout(3000); shot('ending')\\n    check('the ending', snap()['scene'] == 'ending', snap())\\n    for i in range(8): page.keyboard.press('Enter'); page.wait_for_timeout(500)\\n    check('the credits', snap()['scene'] == 'credits', snap()); page.wait_for_timeout(2500); shot('credits')\\n    page.keyboard.press('Enter'); page.wait_for_timeout(1500)\\n    check('back to the title', snap()['scene'] == 'title', snap())\\n    check('no page or game errors', not errs and not ev('My3D2dge.current.errors.length'), errs[:5])\\n    b.close()\\nsrv.terminate()\\nprint('teleports used (walls in the straight line):', teleports)\\nprint('FAILED: ' + ', '.join(fails) if fails else 'browser playthrough complete')\\nsys.exit(1 if fails else 0)\\nEOF\\nnode build.mjs >/dev/null && timeout 900 python3 test/browser_play.py chromium 2>&1 | tail -40\",\"descri