 4096 Nov  2 18:13 ..\\ndrwxr-xr-x 7 micha micha    4096 Nov  2 18:49 Rewired-TheWire-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181307\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 1449116 Nov  2 18:55 Rewired-TheWire-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181307.html\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha    7933 Nov  2 18:13 TASK.md\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha    5645 Nov  2 18:57 exit-interview.json\\n0\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_0177rcTP4c54x9L4weDURFzQ\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181307__x22cc1b/work/exit-interview.json","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":50,"lines":["+{","+  \"sourceInformation\": {","+    \"date\": \"2026-11-02 18:13\",","+    \"source\": \"The Wire (HBO, 2002-2008), created by David Simon; kept as gritty and real as the show\",","+    \"genre\": \"Surveillance and stealth investigation, with a case-board puzzle, a wiretap listening game and a foot chase\",","+    \"perspective\": \"The engine's three-quarter view (pitch 55) as the main view; the player can switch to isometric or top-down at any time\",","+    \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge v0.85.1 (full engine edition, one file, no dependencies); AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client 1.3.0 (session.js); plain JavaScript bundled into one HTML file by a Node build script\",","+    \"artDirection\": \"The engine's native retro-modern pixel look: 320x240 base expanded to any screen, HD Humanoid rigs, TileMap rowhouses with per-pixel painted brick, formstone, boarded vacants and graffiti, objects as data (cars, dumpster, couch, payphone, desks, reel decks), canvas lighting with street lamps, rain at night\",","+    \"animation\": \"The engine's procedural Humanoid rigs driven by velocity and poses, the Mover for the player (sprint, sneak, vault), scene transitions and tweens; no frame lists\",","+    \"audio\": \"Code-written chip-synth music (title blues, corner boom-bap, night, wire room, chase, office, ending), code-written sound effects (shutter, whistle, pager, ram, siren, cuffs), and gibberish Simlish-style voices with a pitch and timbre per speaker, blipped as the text types\",","+    \"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode: each player runs their own seeded 3-minute surveillance shift, the other detectives show as ghosts with names and scores, and progress and score results go to the hub. Local 1-2 player drop-in outside the hub\",","+    \"testing\": \"Headless Node tests (a full five-tape playthrough with 49 checks, 52 system checks, a 16-scene smoke test); Playwright screenshots in Chromium, Firefox and WebKit; viewport-matrix on 24 phone, tablet and desktop configurations; the AI Hub harness with 1, 2 and 4 players, latency, jitter, loss and host-leave\",","+    \"research\": \"None beyond the engine and hub documentation; details of the show from memory\",","+    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\",","+    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",","+    \"usage\": \"unknown\"","+  },","+  \"testingFeedback\": [","+    \"28 issues, found by the headless playthrough and system tests, the browser screenshots and the viewport matrix. The AI Hub harness passed on its first run.\",","+    \"5 critical: a boot step that crashed the start, a runner whose stash spot was inside a wall (the corner stalled forever), a dialog carried into the next scene that froze it, the shift mode triggering story events, and a sale timer left over from the tail that meant later sessions had no sales.\",","+    \"The scripted headless playthrough of all five tapes. It drives the real scenes through game.advance and game.debug, and it found every soft-lock in the story chain.\",","+    \"The viewport matrix: 24 of 24 clean on the first run, because the engine's expand mode already fits every screen. It only caught a toast overlapping the objective box on narrow screens.\"","+  ],","+  \"engineFeedback\": [","+    \"The standard features are already built: the pause menu, rebinding, button glyphs per device, settings that save, fixed-step determinism, and a headless mode where the same game runs in Node for tests.\",","+    \"Several guesses: whether an intent object passed to Mover.update uses ground or screen directions (ground), what a face painter returns for the base colour (null), that objects as data are written facing south (my cars came out sideways at first), and that TileMap.bounds needs a view object, not a view name.\",","+    \"The surveillance layer: a camera viewfinder in world space that works with the mouse, a stick and the keys; the sale cycle that photos are judged against; and the lookouts' suspicion with blending.\",","+    \"Working with a 1.2 MB engine through its index, without seeing pixels quickly. The per-pixel wall painter's signature also takes time to learn.\",","+    \"The loosely checked option objects on draw calls: a typo in an option key is silently ignored.\",","+    \"Ship PlayStation and Xbox button symbols as font glyphs, so prompts drawn with E.font can show them without custom drawing.\"","+  ],","+  \"promptFeedback\": [","+    \"It is specific about the player's experience (a 10-foot UI, glyphs that follow the last device, an attract mode, the touch-only notice) and leaves the genre and design open.\",","+    \"'Follow the hub for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own' can be read as hub only, or as hub plus local multiplayer. I did both.\",","+    \"Fitting the show's slow, procedural texture (paperwork, waiting, minimization) into mechanics that are still fun in a short demo.\",","+    \"A real DualSense on a real TV at ten feet, to judge text size and glyph readability with human eyes.\"","+  ],","+  \"aiHub\": {","+    \"name\": \"REWIRED\",","+    \"tagline\": \"Walk the corner. Build the board. Work the wire.\",","+    \"description\": \"An original surveillance game in the spirit of The Wire: blend in on a West Baltimore corner, photograph hand-to-hands, pin evidence to a case board and minimize calls on a wiretap. In a hub round, everyone works the same corner for one shift.\",","+    \"type\": \"Game\",","+    \"genre\": \"Stealth\",","+    \"source\": \"The Wire\",","+    \"series\": \"\",","+    \"players\": \"1–4\",","+    \"controls\": \"Left stick or WASD to move, L2 or right mouse to raise the camera, R2 or left click for a photo, Circle or C to crouch, Cross or E to interact\",","+    \"tags\": [\"story\", \"stealth\", \"pixel art\", \"crime\", \"three-quarter\", \"co-op\"]","+  }","+}"]}],"created":true},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181313__x3ec78e/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":963,"oldLines":3,"newStart":963,"newLines":6,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CgfAWuAszj3Jj1HZwvfym\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1747,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":409784,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":1747,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"70b9b3fb-a482-4430-a756-95fe6fe59945\",\"uuid\":\"f619020d-3319-4ac1-8781-c52bd6b42fd0\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-03T01:57:17.836Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CgfAWtkLcsR4GgVrJuTi8\",\"thinking_duration_ms\":2038,\"thinking_display\":\"updates\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CgfAWuAszj3Jj1HZwvfym\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"All three choice paths and the systems suite pass. Updating the feedback (pathfinding was a 13th issue, and a 4th soft-lock), then the final browser and hub check on the shipped bundle.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1747,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":409784,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":1747,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"70b9b3fb-a482-4430-a756-95fe6fe59945\",\"uuid\":\"640683d1-9e80-49a4-9786-069d3c9f848a\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-03T01:57:17.837Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CgfAWtkLcsR4GgVrJuTi8\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CgfAWuAszj3Jj1HZwvfym\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01MTwNAJXCrBgbtZcwmDvZCd\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181313__x3ec78e/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport json\\nfb=json.load(open('/tmp/x3ec78e/fb.json'))\\nfb['testing'][0]=fb['testing'][0].replace(\\\"Twelve game issues, plus five mistakes in my own tests.\\\",\\\"Thirteen game issues, plus six mistakes in my own tests.\\\").replace(\\\"The game issues: \\\",\\\"The game issues: foes and allies walked in straight lines, so a goon and Sal could get stuck on opposite sides of a building; \\\")\\nfb['testing'][1]=\\\"Four would have broken the game: the panic attack that never fired (it soft-locks chapter one), Carmine's surrender (it soft-locks the finale), the straight-line enemies who could get stuck behind a building (they stall a wave), and the missing ready() (AI Hub rounds never start).\\\"\\nfb['testing'][2]=\\\"The headless full-story playthrough: a bot plays New Story through the credits with real input taps, on three different choice paths. It found both soft-locks and the pathfinding bug.\\\"\\njson.dump(fb,open('/tmp/x3ec78e/fb.json','w'))\\nd=json.load(open('exit-interview.json'))\\nd['testingFeedback']=fb['testing']; d['sourceInformation']['testing']=d['sourceInformation']['testing'].replace('on two choice paths','on three choice paths')\\nd['sourceInformation']['usage']=\\\"unknown cost and tokens (no meter in this session); session time about 55 minutes\\\"\\njson.dump(d, open('exit-interview.json','w'), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\\nqs=['How many issues did testing catch?','How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?','What was the most helpful test you ran?','What was the least helpful test you ran?']\\np='TheBaritones-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181313/src/09-about.js'; s=open(p).read()\\na=s.index(\\\"  ['TESTING FEEDBACK'\\\"); b=s.index(\\\"  ['ENGINE FEEDBACK'\\\")\\ns=s[:a]+\\\"  ['TESTING FEEDBACK', [\\\\n    \\\"+',\\\\n    '.join(json.dumps('• '+q+' '+x, ensure_ascii=False) for q,x in zip(qs,fb['testing']))+\\\"\\\\n  ]],\\\\n\\\"+s[b:]\\ns=s.replace(\\\"about 45 minutes\\\",\\\"about 55 minutes\\\").replace(\\\"and a full story playthrough by script\\\",\\\"and a full story playthrough by script on three choice paths\\\")\\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\\nEOF\\npython3 -c \\\"import json;json.load(open('exit-interview.json'));print('json ok')\\\"; cd TheBaritones-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181313 && node build.mjs && node tests/systems.mjs | tail -1 && python3 tests/browser.py \\\"http://127.0.0.1:8731/TheBaritones-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181313.html\\\" chromium | tail -1 && cp ../TheBaritones-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181313.html /tmp/x3ec78e/hubtest/game.html && tim