 boss fight, the AI Hub ready() call sat on a game timer that the scene change cleared, you couldn't get out of a reversing car, moving the mouse didn't switch the prompts to the mouse, touch-only phones weren't detected in WebKit and Firefox, the pixel font had no middle dot, the therapy clock sat under the corner buttons, the moon sat under the phone menu button, banners covered fights, the SUV looked like a fridge, and Donna couldn't be clicked.\",","-    \"• How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking? Three would have broken the game: the panic attack that never fired (it soft-locks chapter one), Carmine's surrender (it soft-locks the finale), and the missing ready() (AI Hub rounds never start).\",","-    \"• What was the most helpful test you ran? The headless full-story playthrough: a bot plays New Story through the credits with real input taps, on two different choice paths, and it found both soft-locks.\",","+    \"• How many issues did testing catch? Thirteen game issues, plus six mistakes in my own tests. The game issues: foes and allies walked in straight lines, so a goon and Sal could get stuck on opposite sides of a building; the scripted panic attack never fired (stress drained to 99.9 before the check), Carmine's surrender never set the flag that ends the boss fight, the AI Hub ready() call sat on a game timer that the scene change cleared, you couldn't get out of a reversing car, moving the mouse didn't switch the prompts to the mouse, touch-only phones weren't detected in WebKit and Firefox, the pixel font had no middle dot, the therapy clock sat under the corner buttons, the moon sat under the phone menu button, banners covered fights, the SUV looked like a fridge, and Donna couldn't be clicked.\",","+    \"• How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking? Four would have broken the game: the panic attack that never fired (it soft-locks chapter one), Carmine's surrender (it soft-locks the finale), the straight-line enemies who could get stuck behind a building (they stall a wave), and the missing ready() (AI Hub rounds never start).\",","+    \"• What was the most helpful test you ran? The headless full-story playthrough: a bot plays New Story through the credits with real input taps, on three different choice paths. It found both soft-locks and the pathfinding bug.\",","     \"• What was the least helpful test you ran? The viewport matrix: 24 clean screenshots of the title with no overflow and no errors. It's reassuring, but the game draws on one canvas, so it couldn't find much.\"","   ]],","   ['ENGINE FEEDBACK', ["]}]}],"moreFiles":37,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181307__x22cc1b/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181307__x22cc1b/work/exit-interview.json","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181313__x3ec78e/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181313__x3ec78e/work/TheBaritones-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181313.html","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181313__x3ec78e/work/TheBaritones-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181313/dist/game.js","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181313__x3ec78e/work/TheBaritones-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181313/src/09-about.js","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181313__x3ec78e/work/exit-interview.json","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work/TheSopraniacs-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181316.html","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium__20261102-181316__x96eb17/work/TheSopraniacs-TheSopranos-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261102-181316/index.html","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medi